From 053d2bdc5b275f5b316440321f31e71d15367605 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ajensenwaud <ajensenwaud@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 13:20:11 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 05/29] inkling2: run Mini's loop in the forward

The forward walks the visit plan instead of the layers: 48 visits for
Mini, each with its own cache slot (KV rings and conv states), passes 2
and 3 starting again from the prelude's hidden state and blocks, and the
previous pass's bank (layer 12's input and its output) feeding the q, k,
v and MLP message gates on every core visit. A message visit's mixes run
unnormed (tf_ink2_loop_mix), the gates blend them, and the input norms
follow (tf_ink2_loop_norm). Cache slots, conv rewind sites and kept
states count visits; Small's plan is its layers in order, so its slots,
allocations and launches are unchanged. The server reads inkling2_loop
configs; Mini's four-tap drafter is not wired yet and is skipped.
tf-inkling2-cuda takes --zero-messages as the planted control.
